.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-KEYGEN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-keygen
.Nd make a signature or KEM key pair
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis keygen
.Fl a Ar alg
.Fl o Ar key
.Op Fl -seed Ar hex | file
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis keygen
makes a key pair for
.Ar alg ,
writes the secret key to
.Ar key
(created owner-only, mode 0600) and the public key to
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
Both are key files in the format described in
.Xr noqtis 1 .
It prints one line naming the algorithm and both files.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a Ar alg , Fl -alg Ns = Ns Ar alg
A signature or KEM algorithm, by any name
.Xr noqtis-algs 1
lists; case does not matter.
.It Fl o Ar key , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret key file; the public key goes to
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl -seed Ar hex | file
Deterministic key generation from the standard's seed, for test vectors
and reproducible keys.
When a file of that name exists, its raw bytes (1 to 256) are the seed;
otherwise the argument must be an even number of hex digits.
The seed must have the standard's length: 32 bytes (xi) for ML-DSA;
3n bytes (SK.seed || SK.prf || PK.seed) for SLH-DSA, that is 48, 72 or 96;
64 bytes (d || z) for ML-KEM; 32 bytes for HQC.
A seed of another length is a library error (exit 2).
Anyone who knows the seed knows the secret key.
A seed given as hex digits on the command line can be read by other users
(the process list) and is kept in shell history; prefer a seed file with
mode 0600.
.Nm noqtis keygen
prints a warning when given one.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace existing files.
The old files are removed first.
.El
.Pp
The secret key is written with mode 0600 and the public key with 0644,
whatever the umask: the public key is a trust anchor, and must not be
writable by others.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 on a usage error, an unknown algorithm, a seed of the wrong
length, an existing file without
.Fl -force ,
or a file that cannot be written.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A signing key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me
ML-DSA-65 key pair: me (secret), me.pub (public)
$ head -1 me.pub
noqtis-key-1 ML-DSA-65 pub
.Ed
.Pp
A deterministic ML-DSA-44 key from a 32-byte seed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ml-dsa-44 -o det --seed \e
    000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f101112131415161718191a1b1c1d1e1f
ML-DSA-44 key pair: det (secret), det.pub (public)
.Ed
.Pp
A KEM key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-KEM-768 -o box
ML-KEM-768 key pair: box (secret), box.pub (public)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-algs 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-enc 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 ,
.Xr nqenc 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
